{% set local_problem %}
<p>Alabama's humidity takes a toll on fascia boards, and Hartselle is no exception. When gutters clog or leak, water runs behind them and soaks into the fascia. In our humid climate, that moisture creates perfect conditions for rot, mold, and wood-destroying insects.</p>

<p>The <a href="/recent-projects/">historic homes downtown</a> are particularly vulnerable. Many have original fascia boards weathered by decades of exposure. Even well-maintained wood eventually succumbs to our climate, and any gutter problems accelerate the deterioration.</p>

<p>We've worked on homes throughout Hartselle long enough to know that fascia problems are common — and commonly missed. Homeowners call about gutter issues, and we find the real problem is the rotted wood behind the gutters. You can't fix the gutter problem without fixing the fascia first.</p>

<p>The good news: caught early, fascia repair is straightforward and affordable. Left alone, rot spreads to rafters and roof structure — turning a manageable repair into a major project.</p>

<p><strong>The uncomfortable truth:</strong> About 40% of gutter replacement jobs in Hartselle need some fascia work. Not the whole house — usually isolated sections where gutters leaked or overflowed consistently. We'd rather tell you upfront than install new gutters on compromised wood that won't hold them.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>We start with thorough inspection — checking fascia and soffit for water damage, soft spots, and rot. We'll show you exactly what we find and explain what needs repair. No exaggeration, no unnecessary work, no scare tactics.</p>

<p><strong>For damaged sections:</strong> We carefully remove existing gutters, cut out rotted wood back to solid material, and install new fascia boards. We use quality primed lumber or composite materials designed for our humid climate.</p>

<p><strong>Material choice matters:</strong> Standard pine fascia lasts maybe 10-12 years in Alabama humidity before showing moisture damage. Composite or treated lumber lasts 20+ years. The upgrade costs 30-40% more but more than doubles the lifespan. For Hartselle homes, where you want work to last, it's worth it.</p>

<p>Everything gets properly sealed and prepped for gutter installation. Then we install your new seamless gutters on fresh fascia — properly attached with hangers at 24-inch intervals, properly sloped for drainage, designed to prevent the overflow that caused the rot originally.</p>

<p><strong>What we won't do:</strong> Slap new gutters on damaged fascia just to close the sale. Some gutter companies ignore fascia problems because they don't do carpentry. We'd rather lose a job than install gutters we know won't last.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've been repairing fascia and installing gutters in Hartselle for over 20 years — longer than anywhere else, because this is home. Our mailing address is P.O. Box 103, right here in town.</p>

<p>When you hire Blue River Gutters, you're hiring your neighbors. We're going to do the job right because that's who we are — and because we'll probably see you around town. That accountability matters, and it's something you only get from a truly local company.</p>

<p><strong>Warning from experience:</strong> If someone offers to install new gutters and says your fascia "looks fine" without actually getting up there and pressing on it, get a second opinion. We've replaced plenty of gutters installed 2-3 years ago on damaged fascia — the original installer either didn't notice or didn't mention it. Now the homeowner pays twice.</p>

<p><strong>Our advice:</strong> If you're replacing gutters and your existing ones have leaked for years, expect some fascia damage. Just the reality of Alabama living. Better to know about it and fix it now than discover it when your new gutters start sagging.</p>
